        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.321,
            0.436,
            0.345
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.3 Decimal Division"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.354,
            0.521,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": "**Example 6:** Anuja has a 3.9 m length of ribbon and she wants to cut it into 10 equal pieces. What is the length of each piece in decimal?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.437,
            0.52,
            0.495
          ],
          "content": "Since there are 10 pieces, we can find the length of each piece by dividing 3.9 by 10."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.495,
            0.349,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "So, what is $3 . 9 \\div 1 0 ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.512,
            0.52,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "Let’s convert 3.9 into fraction $3.9 = \\frac{39}{10}$ Hence, $3 . 9 ~ \\div ~ 1 0$ is the same as dividing $\\frac { 3 9 } { 1 0 }$ by 10."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.597,
            0.522,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": "Recall that, dividing a fraction by a divisor is the same as multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of the divisor. The reciprocal of 10 is ${ \\frac { 1 } { 1 0 } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.694,
            0.47,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\frac{39}{10} \\div 10 = \\frac{39}{40} \\times \\frac{1}{10} = \\frac{39}{100} = 0.39.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.733,
            0.522,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": "Thus, the length of each piece of ribbon is 0.39 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.538,
            0.325,
            0.913,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.776,
            0.846,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": "？ What is the length of each piece if the ribbon is cut into 100 equal pieces? $3.9 \\div 100 = \\frac{39}{10} \\times \\frac{1}{100} = \\frac{39}{1000} = 0.039.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.837,
            0.846,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": "When the ribbon is cut into 100 equal pieces, the length of each piece is 0.039 m."
        },
        {
